; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk
;
; no-fixed-tables-band.fk — the seed's function table GROWS; it is not a wall
; (2026-08-27), and the proof that it mattered is the body's own voice.
;
; FK_FN_CAP (4096 function seats) is the wall that made the flatten table look
; necessary. form-cli's preludes closure needs 4101 seats, so `repl` itself was
; never registered: `printf 'ping\n' | ./form/form-cli` answered `nothing`,
; rc 1, with five [fn-cap] errors above it. The seed's own comments had already
; written this receipt twice — 256 -> 4096 on 2026-07-02 after a 258-defn chain
; returned garbage. Growth ends the series. The fn-value sentinel band tracks
; the live capacity (fk_is_fnval), so the encoding stays collision-proof.
;
; The record store (FK_RECORD_CAP 256 / FK_RECORD_MAX_KEYS 128) grew in the
; same sitting — the literal died loud at both caps while record_set silently
; dropped key 129. That heal is NOT asserted here: fkwu's parser mints no
; record-literal node (grep: no tag-64 mint), so records reach this arm only
; through images and a source band cannot honestly exercise it. Named pending
; rather than claimed.
;
; PROOF LEVEL: FOURTH-ARM ONLY — an fkwu seed capacity; the sibling kernels
; carry no such table. Run:
;   ./fkwu form/form-stdlib/tests/no-fixed-tables-band.fk
;
; Bits (power-of-two weights):
;   1  a 4600-defn program registers past the old 4096 seat wall and its LAST
;      defn answers 4600 (= 1 + 4599) — the seat that used to be refused
;   2  the body SPEAKS through the source runner: printf 'ping' into
;      ./form/form-cli answers pong, no flatten table anywhere in the path
; witnessed: 2026-08-28 -> 3
(do
    (defn nft-line-go (s i n)
        (if (ge i n) (substring s 0 n)
            (if (eq (str_byte_at s i) 10) (substring s 0 i)
                (nft-line-go s (add i 1) n))))
    (defn nft-line (s) (if (nothing? s) "" (nft-line-go s 0 (str_len s))))

    (let seats (host-exec "awk 'BEGIN{printf \"(do \"; for(i=0;i<4600;i++) printf \"(defn nftq%d (x) (add x %d))\", i, i; printf \"(nftq4599 1))\"}' > form-stdlib/.cache/nft-seats.fk && ./fkwu form-stdlib/.cache/nft-seats.fk 2>/dev/null; rm -f form-stdlib/.cache/nft-seats.fk form-stdlib/.cache/nft-seats.fkb form-stdlib/.cache/nft-seats.sym" ""))
    (let c0 (if (eq (str_to_int (nft-line seats)) 4600) 1 0))

    (let voice (host-exec "printf 'ping\n' | ./form/form-cli 2>/dev/null" ""))
    (let c1 (if (str_eq (nft-line voice) "pong") 2 0))

    (add c0 c1))
